user_reviews_extended.Description:
This is quite a place.

Lots of pluses:
- the on-boarding and scheduling was easy...their automated system even made finding the place and signing in easy;
- the initial consult was thorough and involved tech solutions (e.g., 3D imaging) that helped with decision-making;
- the team was open to input and created alternative options (along with pricing and referrals);
- the cleaning was fast;
- the staff was all very friendly
- Most importantly, I got more time and conversation with the doctor than I have at previous dentists.

(Last but not least: their swag bag put their money where my mouth was, so to speak.) An overall stellar first experience, which is pretty hard to pull off - impressive.

Hsu and his staff are a group of wonderful people. They can make you feel at ease with all they do. I heard a child in the room next to me who was not at all to sure what to think. But, they had her laughing and talking in no time. They inform you what they have found what it is they have to do to take care of it and hold on to your seats they do it there!!!  That’s a big win in my book. I really do like this dentist and his staff. Thank you all so much. I’ll see you all on my next appointment. 😇

As for my past experiences with other dentists;

I’ve had other dentists and staff make it feel like having an appointment was bothersome and then not providing the right treatment such as taking care of cavities. I was told well they aren’t that bad we will look at them again in a few months. Geez! Or you need an extraction but we don’t do it here so you need to go to this other office. I don’t have time to drive into Georgetown, Roundrock or even into Austin to get another procedures done.
